{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\nClosing satiated-unrideable-tapeworm (Gerrit 1809, merged 42cd70b889) left three residual sub-clauses that are test/reporting hardening, not behavior gaps — all behavior is merged, tested observable-behaviour-style, and CI-green. This ticket carries the remainder so the parent could close honestly.\n\n## Scope (from the parent's AC1-AC3 residuals; full tables in the parent's close-out comment)\n1. AC1 residual: add call-count/monkeypatch assertions on the shared confirmation reduce path so a future regression that bypasses the shared seam (printing per-verb again) is caught structurally, not just per-verb by exact-line tests.\n2. AC2 residual: ship the verb inventory table (no-op-capable vs always-writes) as generated or hand-maintained documentation (docs/cli-reference or a test-enforced table), so the no-op contract is enumerable.\n3. AC3 residual: record the per-verb old→new confirmation-line mapping (the parent's comment has the full table) in docs or the test suite as golden data.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] Reduce-path structural assertion exists (call-count or seam-spy) covering at least create/link/transition.\n- [x] Verb inventory (no-op-capable vs always-writes) lives in a durable, reviewable location and a test fails when a verb is added without classification.\n- [x] Old→new mapping table recorded in docs or golden test data.\n- [x] make lint / make typecheck clean; lands via Gerrit."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787190186613776001,"uuid":"ab0ac844-ddfb-42f5-a0e6-13c94509e523"}